cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenTendonHand in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenTendonHand: An Open-Source High-DOF Tendon-Driven Dexterous Hand"
abstract: >-
  OpenTendonHand is an open-source dexterous robotic hand built around a
  tendon-driven architecture: actuators are mounted in the forearm and
  Bowden-cable routing transmits motion into 20+ degrees of freedom in the
  fingers. The project publishes mechanical CAD, electronics, firmware and
  control software under open licenses.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OpenTendonHand Contributors"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Artree021/OpenTendonHand"
url: "https://github.com/Artree021/OpenTendonHand"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
keywords:
  - dexterous hand
  - robotic hand
  - tendon-driven
  - cable-driven
  - underactuated
  - open hardware
  - robotics
